## Core Concepts

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **Prospect** | An individual person (lead) at a target company. Has job title, email, LinkedIn URL, and seniority level. |
| **Company** | A business entity in the database, identified by domain, with firmographic data (industry, employees, revenue, location). |
| **Signal** | A real-time buying trigger or event associated with a company or prospect — e.g., a new funding round, hiring activity, or technology adoption. |
| **Intent Data** | Bombora-powered behavioral data showing which topics a company is actively researching online. |
| **Campaign** | A structured outreach sequence targeting a list of prospects or companies, via email and/or LinkedIn. |
| **AI Agent** | A specialized AI-powered workflow within Outmate that performs complex research or analysis tasks autonomously. |
| **Credits** | The usage-based currency inside Outmate. Each search query or enrichment action deducts credits from your balance. New accounts start with 100 free credits. |
| **ICP (Ideal Customer Profile)** | The definition of the perfect target company/persona for your product. |
| **Enrichment** | Adding additional data (email, phone, firmographics) to an existing prospect or company record. |
| **Firmographics** | Company-level data: industry, employee count, revenue range, HQ location, funding stage. |
| **Technographics** | The technology tools a company is using (e.g., Salesforce, HubSpot, AWS). |
| **GTM (Go-To-Market)** | Strategy and execution for bringing a product to market - includes ICP targeting, messaging, and outreach. |

